# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Bustfile — failure mode contractile for progblocks
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath)
#
# Every declared failure mode should have a recovery path. Status moves:
#   declared -> drilled (probe run) -> verified (recovery confirmed)
#   or -> failing (recovery broken)
#
# Most entries below are `declared`, not `verified` — these are read
# directly from the source on 2026-08-07, not from a lived incident, except
# where a root-cause chain in FACTS.md's "Rehabilitation history" already
# confirms occurrence, or where a fix has landed and the probe now confirms
# the regression guard holds (noted per entry).

@abstract:
Failure modes specific to progblocks: a pre-alpha, dependency-free web
component and a launcher that cannot start the demo server. A previous
fatal link-time load failure (component-fails-to-register, below) and the
former XSS and focus-destroying render path (fixed 2026-10-05) are kept
here only as regression guards. This is a shorter list than a mature repo's Bustfile because the
project is young — but every entry here is grounded in a specific line of
code, not a hypothetical.
@end

## Failure Modes

### component-fails-to-register (RESOLVED)
- description: src/prog-block.js used to import { validateK9 } from k9-validator.js, which exports only K9Validator and defaultValidator; the named-import mismatch was a link-time SyntaxError, so customElements.define('prog-block', ...) never ran and every <prog-block> on index.html was inert. Fixed by importing { defaultValidator } instead. This entry is kept as a regression guard, not a live failure mode.
- run: "! grep -q 'import { validateK9 }' src/prog-block.js"
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: tests/registration.test.js (asserts customElements.get('prog-block') is defined) plus this probe
- recovery: N/A — fixed on branch fix/honest-gates-v2; since 2026-10-05 src/prog-block.js imports nothing. If this probe ever fails again, remove the import and re-run `bun test`.
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 60
- status: verified

### launcher-cannot-start-server
- description: progblocks-launcher.sh cannot start the demo server — REPO_DIR is never populated (so cd "$REPO_DIR" silently no-ops) and the startup-command search requires [ -x "$candidate" ], which is false for a string like "python3 -m http.server", so START_COMMAND is always empty
- run: grep -q 'REPO_DIR=""' progblocks-launcher.sh
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary) — see ../descriptiles/AGENTIC.a2ml / PLAYBOOK.a2ml
- recovery: Run the demo manually — python3 -m http.server 8080, then open index.html. File the {repo-dir}-token-loss bug upstream in launch-scaffolder; do not hand-edit the generated .sh.
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 30
- status: declared

### xss-injection-surface (RESOLVED 2026-10-05)
- description: Variant content used to be read via innerHTML and re-injected as HTML with no escaping, and variable values interpolated unescaped into value="${val}". Fixed on branch feat/render-core-variants-vars: the shadow tree is built with DOM APIs and all author/reader text goes in via textContent. Kept as a regression guard
- run: "! grep -rn '\.innerHTML' src/"
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: tests/component.test.js ("untrusted content is never rendered as markup", four tests, happy-dom) plus this probe
- recovery: N/A — fixed. If this probe ever fails, move the new code back to textContent plus DOM API construction
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 3600
- status: verified

### editing-destroys-focus-and-templates (RESOLVED 2026-10-05)
- description: Editing a variable input used to trigger a full shadowRoot.innerHTML rewrite, destroying the <input> being typed into; separately, the contenteditable editor overwrote variant source with post-interpolation text. Fixed: the shadow tree is built once and patched in place, and the editor was removed as out of charter. Kept as a regression guard
- run: "! grep -q 'shadowRoot.innerHTML' src/prog-block.js"
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: tests/component.test.js ("typing keeps the same input element…") plus this probe
- recovery: N/A — fixed. If this probe ever fails, patch only the changed nodes instead of rebuilding the shadow root
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 3600
- status: verified

### wasm-placeholder-not-webassembly
- description: assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm is a 118-byte ASCII placeholder, not real WebAssembly; the tree-sitter path in a2ml-parser.js is commented out and nothing imports the module
- run: "file assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm | grep -qv 'WebAssembly'"
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)
- recovery: Either vendor a real compiled tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm and un-comment the parse path, or remove the file and stop implying a parser exists
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 7200
- status: declared

### ci-red-since-repo-creation
- description: CI never had a green run from repo creation (2026-07-23) until PR #12 — root causes were the just installer not being on the org's Actions allowlist, missing JS CodeQL coverage, and later a CodeQL default-vs-advanced conflict and workflow-lockfile enforcement
- run: git log --oneline | grep -q 'fix(ci): unblock Actions'
- severity: info
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)
- recovery: Already recovered — see FACTS.md Rehabilitation history table (PR #12, #13, #15, #16). Kept here because startup_failure has flapped on and off since from GitHub-side cohort enforcement, which is external, not a repo defect.
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 0
- status: verified
